==Film==
=== ''El Camino: A Breaking Bad Movie'' (2019) ===
{{Main|El Camino: A Breaking Bad Movie|label1=''El Camino: A Breaking Bad Movie''}}
''El Camino: A Breaking Bad Movie'' is a film written and directed by series creator [[Vince Gilligan]] that serves as a continuation of the television series.<ref name="ElCamino"/> It was released on October 11, 2019, on [[Netflix]] and was broadcast on [[AMC (TV channel)|AMC]] on February 16, 2020.<ref name="ElCamino"/><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/breaking-bad-movie-amc-premiere-date-full-series-marathon-1142131/ |title=Breaking Bad Movie Gets AMC Premiere Date, Following a Full Series Marathon |website=TVLine |first=Matt Webb |last=Mitovich |date=January 7, 2020 |access-date=January 7, 2020}}</ref> The film centers around [[Jesse Pinkman]], and takes place both during his captivity at the hands of the Aryan Brotherhood and after his escape in the [[Felina (Breaking Bad)|''Breaking Bad'' series finale]].<ref name="ElCamino"/>
 
